      "writtenOn": "2026-05-24T09:05:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do we need to set the task id here? `getFetchRefSpecs()` is also used by helper/status paths such as `safeGetFetchRefSpecs()` and `hasSucceeded()`, not only while the fetch task is actively running. Setting the thread-local here may make callers see a task id during refspec evaluation rather than during actual task execution. Could the task id instead be scoped only around the real fetch execution path?",
