      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Do we need to set the task id here? `getFetchRefSpecs()` is also used by helper/status paths such as `safeGetFetchRefSpecs()` and `hasSucceeded()`, not only while the fetch task is actively running.\n\nTrue, however, in the `pull_replication_log` we track all the activity, including the scheduling and evaluation, not just the execution.\nHaving the task id there as well would allow to isolate and split the logs by task id and the associated preparation and finalisation parts, not just the execution.\n\n\u003e Setting the thread-local here may make callers see a task id during refspec evaluation rather than during actual task execution. \n\nTrue, I would prefer to see the associated task id rather than a `null`.\n\n\u003e Could the task id instead be scoped only around the real fetch execution path?\n\nNo, I\u0027d like to see all the way through, also in the preparation and final completion of the fetch task.",
