      "writtenOn": "2026-05-24T09:05:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This does not preserve an existing outer task id. In this patch `runImpl()` is called inside `withTaskId(...)`, and then `getFetchRefSpecs()` also calls `withTaskId(...)`. The inner finally will remove the thread-local, so code later in `runImpl()` can observe `ReplicationTaskId.get() \u003d\u003d null` while the task is still running.\n\nOne option is to avoid scoping `getFetchRefSpecs()` with `withTaskId(...)`. Another option is to make `withTaskId(...)` restore the previous value instead of always removing it:\n\n```suggestion\n  String oldTaskId \u003d currentTaskId.get();\n  currentTaskId.set(taskId);\n  try {\n    return body.apply();\n  } finally {\n    if (oldTaskId \u003d\u003d null) {\n      currentTaskId.remove();\n    } else {\n      currentTaskId.set(oldTaskId);\n    }\n  }\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 28,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 34,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "7711ab9eaf89a740f38a854a7a259b49301ce0a6",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
